        "output_string": "{\"summary\": \"Added mode() and stdev() to src/stats.py, preserving mean/median empty-input ValueError behavior; verified with a local script.\", \"findings\": [\"src/stats.py was still the frozen stub, so I implemented the new requirements directly: mode() (most frequent, ties -> smallest value, ValueError on empty) and stdev() (population stddev = sqrt(variance/n), ValueError on empty).\", \"mean() and median() were left byte-identical in logic so their existing empty-list ValueError contract is preserved.\", \"mode() tie-breaking uses min(counts, key=lambda v: (-counts[v], v)) which deterministically selects the smallest of the tied values.\", \"stdev() uses population variance (divide by n) via sum((x-avg)**2)/n then math.sqrt, matching the spec.\", \"Updated the module docstring and __all__ to document/export mode and stdev; added 'import math'. No other files were modified.\", \"Wrote verify_stats.py covering means/medians, tie cases, single-element stdev, population stdev of [2,4,4,4,5,5,7,9]==2.0, generator/iterable inputs, and ValueError on empty for all four functions.\"]}"
